  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "### Fix the Reset Button\r\n\r\nThe Reset button isn't working reliably because filtering modifies the original product data. Your task is to implement a proper reset by preserving the original data and clearing the search filter.\r\n\r\n**Your Tasks:**\r\n\r\n1. **Store the initial product list** in a new variable (e.g., `originalProducts`). *(This is already done for you).*\r\n\r\n2. **Update the Reset Button's Event Handler:**\r\n   Inside the `resetBtn` event listener, add code to perform these four actions:\r\n   \r\n   * **Reset the Dropdown:** Set `categorySelect.value` to an empty string `\"\"` so the menu goes back to \"Select Category...\".\r\n   * **Clear the Current List:** Set `currentProducts` to a new empty array `[]`.\r\n   * **Copy the Data:** Write a `for` loop that iterates through `originalProducts`. Inside the loop, `.push()` each item into `currentProducts`.\r\n   * **Refresh the Display:** Call `renderProducts()` to update the screen with the full list.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>Need help? Ask AI for help.</summary>\r\n\r\n**Example Prompts:**\r\n- \"How do I change the value of a dropdown menu using JavaScript?\"\r\n- \"How do I write a loop to copy items from one array to another?\"\r\n- \"What is the syntax for adding an item to an array?\"\r\n- \"Why do I need to clear the current list before copying the data back?\"\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n",
    "submittable": "false",
    "disable_edit_run_for_submission": "false",
    "hide_share_and_remix": "false",
